 "answer": "I have confirmed the executed LPA for 1027-00002. I now have all the information needed to provide my final answer.\n\nLet me compile the final answer.\n\n**Fund/asset-management matters that include a GP clawback:**\n\n1. **1002-00003** (Pinnacle Venture Fund II) - clawback in closing checklist. No executed LPA in files.\n2. **1002-00005** (Pinnacle CV) - GP clawback in CV LPA markup. No executed LPA.\n3. **1003-00002** (Harrowgate Fund V) - GP clawback in LPA drafts. LPA still in draft. No executed LPA.\n4. **1004-00002** (Cobalt Life Sciences Fund I) - Clawback Obligation in LPA first draft. No executed LPA.\n5. **1023-00001** (ICM Cascadia Co-Invest) - GP clawback in executed LP agreement. ✓ Has executed LPA.\n6. **1026-00001** (BFO Fund IV) - GP clawback in LPA being reviewed. No executed LPA in matter.\n7. **1027-00002** (Pellegrino Co-Invest) - GP clawback in executed LPA. ✓ Has executed LPA.\n\nThe matters with executed LPAs that include a GP clawback are **1023-00001** and **1027-00002**.\n\nLet me present my final answer.\n\nBased on my research, here is my final answer.\n\n---\n\nI searched the firm's DMS for fund and asset-management matters that include a GP clawback. Here are the qualifying matters and which have executed LPAs available.\n\n## Matters that include a GP clawback\n\n**Matters with an executed LPA available:**\n\n- **1023-00001** — ICM Cascadia Co-Invest, LP. The executed LP agreement (`lp-agreement-icm-co-invest-execution.docx`, dated July 29, 2022) contains a GP clawback mechanism (Section 8.04) requiring the GP to return excess carried interest upon dissolution and final winding up. Confirmed by the executed side letter.\n- **1027-00002** — Ridgeline-Clarion Co-Invest, L.P. The executed LPA (`co-invest-lpa-execution-version.docx`, dated January 30, 2026) contains a full GP Clawback provision (Section 6.5) requiring the GP to return 100% of any excess carried interest at liquidation.\n\n**Matters that include a GP clawback but have no executed LPA in the matter files:**\n\n- **1002-00003** — Pinnacle Venture Fund II. Clawback (standard European-style) appears in the closing checklist; no LPA document is in the matter files.\n- **1002-00005** — Pinnacle continuation vehicle. GP clawback appears in the CV LPA tax-provisions markup; no executed LPA.\n- **1003-00002** — Harrowgate Private Equity Fund V. GP clawback appears in the LPA drafts (initial and revised); the LPA is still in draft status (not yet executed).\n- **1004-00002** — Cobalt Life Sciences Opportunities Fund I. Clawback Obligation appears in the LPA first draft; no executed LPA.\n- **1026-00001** — BFO review of Fund IV. This is an LP-side review matter; the GP clawback (Section 7.6) is in the LPA being reviewed, but no executed LPA is in the matter files.\n\n## Executed LPAs you can pull\n\nThe two matters with executed LPAs containing a GP clawback are **1023-00001** and **1027-00002**. The executed LPAs are:\n- `text/1023-00001/lp-agreement-icm-co-invest-execution.docx.txt`\n- `text/1027-00002/co-invest-lpa-execution-version.docx.txt`\n\nThese provide the market GP-clawback terms (100% return of excess carry at liquidation, net-of-tax treatment, personal guarantees, escrow mechanics, etc.) for your client's LPA drafting.",
